{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122090","id":4202942414,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc76g8_O","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122090","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122090.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122090.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122090","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122090/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122090/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122090/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/072027fa26cee71575ec5c88507af2b79922eb6e","number":122090,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add unit tests for Vector2::orthogonal() and Vector2::is_same()","user":{"login":"blockersiontko","id":282604314,"node_id":"U_kgDOENgzGg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282604314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blockersiontko","html_url":"https://github.com/blockersiontko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blockersiontko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blockersiontko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blockersiontko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blockersiontko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blockersiontko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blockersiontko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blockersiontko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blockersiontko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blockersiontko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nAdds missing unit test coverage for `Vector2::orthogonal()` and `Vector2::is_same()`, which had no tests despite other Vector2 methods being covered.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nContributes to #43440.\r\n\r\nTest coverage added:\r\n- `orthogonal()`: verified against representative vectors including the zero vector, matching the `Vector2(y, -x)` formula.\r\n- `is_same()`: verified equality/inequality, and specifically that it treats two NaN components as equal (unlike the `==` operator), matching its underlying `Math::is_same()` implementation.\r\n\r\n## AI disclosure\r\n\r\nI used Claude (Anthropic) as a guide while writing this PR, as this is my first contribution to Godot. Specifically, it helped me:\r\n- Identify which Vector2 methods lacked test coverage by comparing the class header against the existing test file.\r\n- Understand the exact behavior of `orthogonal()` and `is_same()` by walking through their source code (including the underlying `Math::is_same()` helper) with me.\r\n- Match the existing code style/conventions used in `test_vector2.cpp` (CHECK_MESSAGE/CHECK_FALSE_MESSAGE formatting).\r\n\r\nI reviewed, compiled, and ran the resulting tests myself (all 22 test cases pass, 148 assertions) before opening this PR, and understand what the code does.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2231593685,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMjMxNTkzNjg1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:tests","name":"topic:tests","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/go